      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "API DESIGN\n",
      "fontSize": 50.161567244105946,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "API DESIGN\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "M2tHX078Z0sXnOqmkbTnz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -268.8046153488249,
      "y": 328.66785402938046,
      "width": 1305.4786278697866,
      "height": 412.5923343869555,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 912116040,
      "version": 843,
      "versionNonce": 728391948,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787930164445,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "POST /api/urls/shorten\nRequest: Send a Long URL\nResponse: Get a Short URL\n\nGET /api/urls/{shortURL}\nResponse: Redirect 302 to the long URL - This can be cached in HTTP \nif not taken for analytics\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36.674874167729385,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "POST /api/urls/shorten\nRequest: Send a Long URL\nResponse: Get a Short URL\n\nGET /api/urls/{shortURL}\nResponse: Redirect 302 to the long URL - This can be cached in HTTP \nif not taken for analytics\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "QWLloQ_RO5bTOvK1tXjss",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -303.6524154884061,
      "y": 787.5323605089535,
      "width": 483.24591499405574,
      "height": 57.92095021100389,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 891533128,
      "version": 551,
      "versionNonce": 2136067640,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787864696747,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HIGH LEVEL DESIGN",
      "fontSize": 46.33676016880311,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HIGH LEVEL DESIGN",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-eU_WgzWb38r8RCJx0z5i",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -338.52195950500357,
      "y": 874.9620684297358,
      "width": 2708.497314453125,
      "height": 1332.1818548530894,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1368858952,
      "version": 2894,
      "versionNonce": 1110839988,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787930289755,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- We can use one service for both redirection and shortening \nbut it is better to decouple them.\n- Use a API Gateway to route the API requests to the correct service. \nThis way client does not need to know about the services.\n- A simple relational Database can be used, a shortURL + longURL can be 1kb.\n- Total records could be 1kb * 1 TB = 5 TB so one database is enough.\n- We can use REDIS for a Counter Service, it is single threaded so it can avoid\nconcurrency issues. But this could become a single point of failure.\n- We can assign random URLs through Hashing. \nIf there are collisions, we can just retry. This works in a real world and will \nprobably take less than 5 seconds to create one short URL\n- To increase read throughput, we can cache the most frequently used short URLs\nand improve latency.\n- We can increase the Counter inside the Redirection service so everytime we redirect,\nwe just increase the count in the database.\n- We can also create another analytics service, add the count in memory and \nflush the data back to DB periodically using a cron job.\n- On every read, check the difference from the createdDate and do not return if the URL is expired\n- Get the Expiry date from the interviewer and automatically delete records from the DB using a worker\n- We have a DB replica, anytime the main DB goes down, we can promote this as the main DB.\n- Check submitted URLs against a safe-browsing/blocklist API at creation time, reject or flag known-malicious domains \n\n",
      "fontSize": 46.33676016880311,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- We can use one service for both redirection and shortening \nbut it is better to decouple them.\n- Use a API Gateway to route the API requests to the correct service. \nThis way client does not need to know about the services.\n- A simple relational Database can be used, a shortURL + longURL can be 1kb.\n- Total records could be 1kb * 1 TB = 5 TB so one database is enough.\n- We can use REDIS for a Counter Service, it is single threaded so it can avoid\nconcurrency issues. But this could become a single point of failure.\n- We can assign random URLs through Hashing. \nIf there are collisions, we can just retry. This works in a real world and will \nprobably take less than 5 seconds to create one short URL\n- To increase read throughput, we can cache the most frequently used short URLs\nand improve latency.\n- We can increase the Counter inside the Redirection service so everytime we redirect,\nwe just increase the count in the database.\n- We can also create another analytics service, add the count in memory and \nflush the data back to DB periodically using a cron job.\n- On every read, check the difference from the createdDate and do not return if the URL is expired\n- Get the Expiry date from the interviewer and automatically delete records from the DB using a worker\n- We have a DB replica, anytime the main DB goes down, we can promote this as the main DB.\n- Check submitted URLs against a safe-browsing/blocklist API at creation time, reject or flag known-malicious domains \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
